/**
 * @page topic_winget Windows package managers
 *
 * @brief Installing ascii-chat and libasciichat through Windows package managers.
 *
 * The release workflow publishes x64 and ARM64 ZIP archives, plus an x64 WiX
 * MSI. The package-manager workflow runs after a successful release, or can be
 * run manually for any release tag, and updates WinGet, Scoop, Chocolatey,
 * and the publisher-hosted Npackd repository.
 *
 * To enable the automated submissions, add a repository secret named
 * `PACKAGE_MANAGER_GITHUB_TOKEN`. The token needs permission to push to the
 * publisher's package repositories and open upstream pull requests. The
 * default repositories are `zfogg/winget-pkgs`, `zfogg/ascii-chat-scoop`,
 * `zfogg/chocolatey-packages`, and `zfogg/npackd-repository`.
 *
 * After Microsoft's manifest review merges the initial submission, users can
 * install and update ascii-chat with:
 *
 * @code{.ps1}
 * winget install ascii-chat
 * scoop bucket add ascii-chat https://github.com/zfogg/ascii-chat-scoop
 * scoop install ascii-chat/ascii-chat
 * choco install ascii-chat
 * ncl add-repo https://raw.githubusercontent.com/zfogg/npackd-repository/master/repository.xml
 * ncl add ascii-chat
 * @endcode
 *
 * WinGet and Scoop expose ARM64 where supported. Chocolatey selects the x64
 * or ARM64 ZIP at install time. Npackd represents ARM64 as the explicit
 * `ascii-chat-arm64` and `libasciichat-arm64` package IDs because its
 * repository format has no general architecture selector.
 */
